y the tagline of the brand also  under the video suggested that they  wanted to celebrate what they called  the confluence between two different  religions their cultures and traditions  but there's been a massive backlash to  this and critics  attribute this outrage to what they say  is a deep-seated intolerance towards  anything which promotes interfaith  harmony  over the past few years but the  overarching idea  is that any content or any agenda which  talks which is liberal or secular and  talks about  harmony is basically done at the expense  of the sentiments of the hindus which  form the majority of the country  and people who are against this ad who  have been trending boycott  tanishq which is the brand name on  social media saying that this ad  glorifies  what they call love jihad what is this  term love jihad it keeps coming up in  some of the tweets that we have also  shown to our viewers it is there across  social media what exactly is it what is  its  genesis  love jihad basically is understood to be  a hindu fundamentalist conspiracy theory  in which  which alleges that muslim men are  engaged into this conspiracy of  converting hindu women to islam  by marrying them so certain cases in the  past over many years have been picked up  by sometimes fringe elements of local  political parties or even media  to portray the mass cases of love jihad  but they have been probes  uh into this case as well in which  interfaith marriages have been probed  and  agencies have found absolutely no  evidence of love jihad  in which hindu women are being  understood to be being maltreated or  suffer in these marriages but from  everything that you're saying manira it  sounds like there is a religious divide  in india how deep is it  well the hindu muslim divide and the  tensions which follow are nothing new to  india we have seen these issues spring  up over the past many years  at different times in different ways but  critics say that this deep-seated  intolerance towards anything which  promotes  the hindu muslim harmony has faced a lot  of opposition especially under the  current ruling party  which even though the ruling  establishment the main leadership line  has never said so in so many words but  there has been an  understanding that the ruling party  plans more towards the majoritarian view  of the country  and critics say that this idea of  intolerance has been played up by  playing on the sense of hindus feeling  the injustice  as they feel that their interests have  played a second fiddle to those of  muslims especially under the previous  governments  so then does that mean that this is the  end of this particular controversy in  relation to this advertisement  it does look like because the brand has  taken down the advertisement they have  even published a statement that why they  had to take down the advertisements  and also there have been news reports of  the shops of this particular particular  brand being attacked in different parts  of the country  so clearly the social media outrage  which followed  this advertisement over the past couple  of days did push the brand to take this  major step  of actually pulling down the  advertisement and sharing the statement  regarding that  we leave it there for the time being but  thank you so much for joining us manira  chaudhary from delhi
 

